BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T163000
UID:6a31e2f290cc4e3a790eabfe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a31e2f290cc4e3a790eabfe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3D Design with Onshape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T200000
UID:6a31e34d43b41b3d006efaa3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to create parametric designs using cloud based softw
 are Onshape.\nThis hands-on workshop introduces participants to the fundam
 entals of 3D design using Onshape\, a cloud-based CAD software. Whether yo
 u're an aspiring engineer\, designer\, or hobbyist\, this session provides
  the tools and knowledge to start creating your own 3D models.\nWhat You
 ’ll Learn:\nGetting Started:\nOverview of Onshape's interface\, navigati
 on tools\, and cloud-based collaboration features.\nCore Design Principles
 :\nUnderstanding 3D modeling basics\, including sketches\, extrusions\, an
 d revolutions.\nHands-On Practice:\nCreating simple 3D parts\, assembling 
 components\, and exploring design modifications.\nBest Practices:\nTips fo
 r efficient modeling\, managing design iterations\, and exporting models f
 or 3D printing or other applications.\nThis program is ideal for beginners
  with no prior experience in CAD software\, as well as those looking to ex
 plore Onshape's capabilities.\nRegistration will start 2 weeks before this
  class. Computers will be provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
