BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Asefeh Katoozian
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a469df04407827f8aa8e2f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, the works of artist Asefeh Kato
 ozian are on display at Morningside branch.\nAsefeh is a multidisciplinary
  artist and architect with an interest in philosophy. Her work explores pa
 inting through rhythm\, form\, structure\, and visual language\, focusing 
 on the relationship between composition and perception. She transforms vis
 ual elements into expressive forms that create a dialogue between nature\,
  memory\, and movement. Her practice reflects an ongoing exploration of ho
 w visual experience shapes meaning\, perception\, and inner understanding.
 \n"I explore rhythm\, form\, structure\, and light as guiding elements of 
 artistic expression in my practice. The relationship between these element
 s creates space for introspection and imagination. Through this practice\,
  I shape compositions that investigate how rhythm\, light\, and the Persia
 n alphabet influence my inner journey in the process of creating an artwor
 k."\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit program\n. Toronto Public 
 Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at location
 s across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural inte
 rests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed durin
 g Morningside branch's open hours. Please check the\nMorningside\nbranch 
 page before your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Asefeh Kat
 oozian\; "Rhythm Ink on the Paper"\; 19.5 x 24.5
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a469df04407827f8aa8e2f2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
